kerbridge (@VERSION@) unstable; urgency=@URGENCY@

  Every option a config file must set is now a line to complete: commented
  out, under its example and a `# REQUIRED.` note. `kbconfig upgrade` writes
  each file in this shape and carries your own values across, so a set that
  was complete stays complete. A set left on a template's example value --
  the realm EXAMPLE.SITE, the tenant aaaabbbb-0000-cccc-..., a bind DN under
  DC=example,DC=site -- keeps that value, because it is a line you set.
  `kbconfig decisions` lists what your set states.

  The install questions are down to three: the realm, the LDAPS URL, and
  which cloud IdP adapter to write a source file for. The five
  kerbridge-config/* preseed keys naming the tenant, the three applications
  and the admission group are gone. A preseeding deployment writes the set
  with `kbconfig init --set` instead, which can express two sources and
  every option; the questions never could.

  Run `kbconfig upgrade` before you restart the daemon. It removes the
  retired sync.toml options cycle_deadline_seconds and read_deadline_seconds;
  the daemon refuses a file that still names either one.

  It also copies sync.toml's sam_source into every idp_<source>.toml, under
  [provider_config]. No account changes its name; the option only moves.
  The daemon refuses a sync.toml that still names it.

  In idp_<source>.toml, admission_group and device_grant_group are removed.
  Set admission_group_id or device_grant_group_id to the group's Object Id
  (Entra, on the group's Overview page) instead of its name. `kbconfig
  upgrade` cannot make this change, and the daemon refuses a file that still
  names either old option.

  Delete /var/lib/kerbridge/sync/problem-admission-group-misconfigured*.json
  if it exists. Nothing clears it now.

  Delete /var/lib/kerbridge/sync/problem-graph-credential-*.json also. The
  two events are named sync-credential-expiring and sync-credential-expired
  now, so a problem left under the old name never clears. Change any
  monitoring rule that matches the old name.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  @DATE@
